"The Endings have framed Davrar since its making; the original Questors predate the first."
"Endings exist to clear the board, prevent overpopulation and bring in new powers."
"Elders think unchecked civilizations become conquering empires or ossify and collapse."
"The Endings were meant to stress-test cultures and reset Davrar to a baseline."
"An Ending removed the overbearing gods."
"The Endings would likely go on even if every Questor left Davrar."
"After the Ending of Magic, a Conclave vote to end the Endings and mind magic failed."
"Nuclear fission has been a restricted secret since the Ending of Magic."
"Questors have lived through a dozen Endings; Sarya through eight."
"Questors wrote off antimagic as a Path five Endings ago."
"A few hundred years ago a Conclave won Staggered Endings in place of a greater demand."
"Staggered Endings let an Ending be shifted in time so people can flee between continents."
"The Ending of History was due for Gemore about a thousand years off."
"Badud traded three continents and 1500 years of non-interference to bring it early."
"By that deal the Ending of History will hit Gemore within about a hundred years."
"Stella feared that breaking Seals could bring an Ending of Silence."
"Years later the Heirs swore an oath on the Gemore Seal to end the Endings."
"Years later Colborn opened a great Conclave calling the Endings a ceiling on meaning."
"Years later the Continuance Charter passed, replacing Endings with events that bring new magics."
"The Charter's aims: spontaneous dungeons, blights with agency and a monster ecology."
"The Charter also set rules for wars and civilian zones immune to mass spells."
"The Charter banned mind magics, contract magics and mass social skills."
"After the Charter, monsters grew less aggressive and gained creature needs."
